WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.340
Venezuela is undergoing some of its worst
moments.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.290
This disaster is so huge, that what once was
one of the largest and most powerful oil companies

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:14.620
in the world, PDVSA, is now practically bankrupt
and has more problems, including extracting

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:15.620
oil.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:21.069
One second, the oil company with the largest
reserves in the world has problems extracting

00:00:21.069 --> 00:00:22.069
it?

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:28.630
Yes, you heard that right, and we’ll tell
you all about it in this video…

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:39.720
Folks, I think we all know it: Venezuela is
undergoing a true catastrophe, and not only

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.720
an economic one.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:48.980
It is, above all, humanitarian.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:53.690
Such a huge disaster that in recent years
it has caused between 3 and 4 million Venezuelans

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.690
to flee the country.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:57.540
That is, more than 1 in 10 inhabitants.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.750
And the truth is… we’re not surprised.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:05.720
See, according to the latest statistics, 87%
of the population, 87%, almost 9 out of every

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.979
10 Venezuelans, are poor...

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:12.549
And, on top of that, most of Venezuela’s
population, 60%, isn’t only poor, they live

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:16.869
in extreme poverty.

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:21.040
But... not only that...

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.939
Venezuela is burning down…

00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:28.639
According to data from the Venezuelan Social
Conflict Observatory, in 2017 almost 10,000

00:01:28.639 --> 00:01:32.459
protests were registered throughout the country,
more than 27 a day.

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:40.679
And what’s even worse:

00:01:40.679 --> 00:01:45.789
According to information from the former Attorney
General, Luisa Ortega, since 2015 the police,

00:01:45.789 --> 00:01:50.060
the National Guard, the Army and the different
intelligence services, have killed more than

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.060
8,000 people.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:56.409
Of course, most of them were regime opposers.

00:01:56.409 --> 00:02:02.040
Crisis, hunger, violence, repression...

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:08.530
everything indicates that Venezuela will soon
undergo a refugee crisis of colossal dimensions.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:13.620
Because dear viewers, let's be honest, things
aren’t looking good at all.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.831
See, for years, the "Bolivarian revolution"
of Chavez, Maduro and company had a great

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:24.200
ally, and we’re not talking about Cuba,
or Russia or any other country, but about

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.320
oil... the black gold that financed the "revolution".

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:33.360
For a long time, the huge income this raw
material brought financed all of the regime’s

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.470
policies, and they didn’t care at all about
the consequences.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:40.140
That is to say, factories were closing?

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.050
Foreign investment was fleeing the country?

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.500
It didn’t matter because, folks, they had
oil dollars.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.500
However...

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.190
all of that is about to end.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.590
Yes, Venezuela has a lot of oil.

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:56.390
But... one thing is having oil and another
quite different thing is being able to exploit

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:57.390
it.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:03.460
Did you know that PDVSA , the national oil
company, is practically about to collapse?

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.100
Listen up.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:12.040
(THE FALL OF PDVSA

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:19.410
Petroleum of Venezuela, PDVSA , was created
by government decree in 1976, to integrate

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:22.850
all the oil assets the State had nationalized...

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:28.240
This company soon became a world-class colossus.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:32.120
Do you know why?

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:37.570
Well, among other things because this company
has the largest reserves on the planet...

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.790
and, we mean large:

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:45.650
there are more than 300 billion barrels of
oil certified, more than the reserves of Saudi

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.150
Arabia, the Emirates, Russia or any other
oil power.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:54.150
Yes, it's true, we've said it here, Venezuelan
oil doesn’t have the highest quality, but...

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.230
it doesn’t matter.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:04:00.650
We’re talking about a huge amount of resources,
almost 20% of all known world reserves.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:07.490
Well, the fact is that this company, PDVSA
, peaked in production in 1998, a year before

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:12.320
Hugo Chávez came to power, at which time
PDVSA was extracting 3 and a half million

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.819
barrels per day.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:16.030
Since then, things have changed a lot.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:21.750
By the year of Hugo Chávez’sdeath in 2013,
production had decreased by 1 million barrels

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:22.910
per day…

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.800
One moment, one million less?

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.410
Could it be that Hugo Chávez’s Bolivarian
government didn’t like oil?

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:33.720
Could it be part of a twisted plan to diversify
the Venezuelan economy?

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.750
Well... no.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:47.010
Quite 
the opposite.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:54.020
Hugo Chávez wanted to increase production
to 5 million barrels.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.840
The problem was that, they simply weren’t
able to do it.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.750
But if you think that the commander’s results
were bad, you haven’t seen anything yet…

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:06.970
Because since Nicolás Maduro came to power,
production has sunk to 1.8 million barrels.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:11.260
That means that, while countries like the
United States have doubled their production,

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:16.440
Venezuela produces half as much oil as when
the revolution began.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.470
Very successful.

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:32.950
And if you think that’s the worst of it,
think again.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:35.510
No, he future looks a lot worse.

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:43.419
Now, at this point, you may be wondering,
what the hell is going on with PDVSA ?

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:49.410
(THE KEYS OF A DISASTER FORETOLD)

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:56.150
The PDVSA’s history, dear viewers, has been
the story of a disaster foretold.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:00.580
The best example is that of the Paraguaná
refining complex, which consists of 3 crude

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:05.910
oil refineries and is one of the 3 largest
complexes of its kind on the entire planet.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.880
For years, it was Venezuela’s industrial
pride, the Crown jewel.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.350
However, today...

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:17.389
it barely operates at 15% capacity... and
all kinds of accidents tend to happen, why?

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:19.460
("There’s no maintenance.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:23.010
They sucked everything they could from PDVSA
without investing, there’s nothing left

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.710
to squeeze" Pablo Céspedes, plant operator.)

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:29.180
And this isn’t some extraordinary case.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:34.370
At the end of October, also in the Paraguaná
refining complex, the Amuay refinery spilled

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.300
over 200,000 gallons of gasoline into the
bay;

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:41.711
a few days later, another refinery in the
complex, the Cardon refinery suffered a fire

00:06:41.711 --> 00:06:46.199
that the firemen could barely contain, because
they didn’t even have foam to fight the

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:49.370
flames.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:51.940
And so on and so on.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:55.639
Because the truth is that most of the oil
company’s facilities are in terrible condition.

00:06:55.639 --> 00:06:56.639
But...

00:06:56.639 --> 00:07:00.419
How do you think they reached this point?

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:13.060
Well, you see, the Chavez government always
saw PDVSA as a kind of dairy cow from which

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:16.409
they could get all the resources they needed
for their "Bolivarian revolution"...

00:07:16.409 --> 00:07:21.810
the problem is that the oil industry requires
lots of investments, investments that the

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:27.210
Venezuelan government simply didn’t want
to make.

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:31.449
Even with the fact that it indebted PDVSA
to the brim.

00:07:31.449 --> 00:07:34.860
By the way, do you know how indebted this
company is today?

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:40.590
Listen to this… we’re not talking about
1 or 5, but 90 billion dollars.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:46.820
A fortune so big that Venezuela could have
even bought multinationals like Goldman Sachs,

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.540
Nike or Siemens.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:53.620
Now that’s a lot of debt!

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:54.620
But...

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:55.830
do you think that’s all?

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:56.900
Not even close.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:08:01.449
They also used the company to plug-in, place
and hire thousands and thousands of supporters,

00:08:01.449 --> 00:08:06.550
friends and family members... from which PDVSA
lost even more resources.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:11.210
And if that weren’t enough, the Chavez regime
also placed unskilled and inexperienced personnel

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:15.620
in management positions, while dismissing
and driving away thousands and thousands of

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.740
experienced employees because of their political
beliefs.

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:23.990
Yes, this is how PDVSA has run out of money
and out of human resources..

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:28.300
Now we can understand why oil production is
dropping.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:35.169
Of course, the consequences of all this are...
terrible for the country.

00:08:35.169 --> 00:08:43.169
(THE CONSEQUENCES)

00:08:43.169 --> 00:08:45.980
Oil is essential for the Venezuelan economy...

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.890
especially because there’s no other industry
left standing.

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:55.490
Their dependence is so great that oil generates
95% of all foreign currency profits, in dollars,

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:56.910
for example.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:01.320
And these currencies, my friends, are what
Venezuela needs to be able to import food,

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:06.440
medicine, gasoline – yes, today Venezuela
has to import gasoline – or anything else.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:07.610
But of course...

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.460
as oil production keeps plummeting…

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:17.350
the country has to import fewer things.

00:09:17.350 --> 00:09:18.350
And you know what?

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:21.850
Since Venezuela is literally producing nothing
and has to import everything, the dwindling

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.890
oil money is no longer enough to pay all the
bills.

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:28.910
But... of course, as you all know, when you
spend more money than you make… money goes

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:32.950
away… and that’s precisely what’s happening
to Venezuela, which according to some calculations,

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:38.790
barely has 10 billion dollars in foreign reserves,
which is their lowest number in 40 years..

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:42.260
This means… that when the money is gone,
they won’t be able to import anything else

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:46.680
than what they can buy with what they make
from the oil… which is decreasing.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:49.620
Do you see the problem?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:56.990
Until now, as we saw here on VISUALPOLITIK,
Nicolás Maduro’s government has tried to

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:00.750
buy time by resorting to international markets
to issue debt...

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.910
at scandalous rates, sometimes as high as
40%.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:09.760
Obviously, issuing debts with implicit rates,
interests of 40% can only mean future ruin.

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.630
And in any case, that is actually no longer
a possibility.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:18.649
In fact, both the Venezuelan government and
PDVSA are incurring defaults, that is, they

00:10:18.649 --> 00:10:21.140
aren’t paying their debts.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:26.580
("S&amp;P downgrades seven sovereign Venezuelan
bonds to the default level" Bank and Business)

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:29.240
Another route they’ve attempted, was that
of the Chinese rescue... and the Chinese answered

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:32.649
and placed more than 23 billion dollars in
loans on the table...

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:33.649
But...

00:10:33.649 --> 00:10:38.930
everything has a limit, and they are no longer
willing to continue giving more money for

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.149
nothing.

00:10:40.149 --> 00:10:41.149
Check this out.

00:10:41.149 --> 00:10:45.550
( "The Chinese oil company Sinopec sues PDVSA
for unpaid debts" OilPrice.)

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:49.500
The situation, my friends, is so desperate
that the Cuban government has decided to seize

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:54.900
the 49% that PDVSA held in a Cuban refinery
as compensation for unpaid debts.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.430
You heard that right,

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:58.600
Not even Cuba trusts the Maduro regime!

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:09.730
And, it was all of this that led to the latest
Chavista event: the Petro.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.640
THE VENEZUELAN CRYPTOCURRENCY

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:17.310
As we’ve seen, with every day that passes
the Venezuelan government has less access

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:21.550
to foreign currency... which is obviously
a huge problem... because without foreign

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:22.850
currency they can’t import.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:26.120
But, based on this problem, an idea came up:

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:32.160
Cryptocurrency is in fashion, so why not launch
their own cryptocurrency?: The Petro.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:34.480
Of course...

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:50.970
the petro is a 

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:55.620
very particular currency... among other things,
because it’s controlled by Maduro’s government.

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.370
Under these conditions, I ask you a question,

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:02.490
Would you be willing to invest a single euro,
a single dollar in this new cryptocurrency?

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:06.050
Or in other words, would you put your money
in the hands of the Venezuelan government?

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:10.340
I know I wouldn’t… not even a penny.

00:12:10.340 --> 00:12:18.730
And precisely because no one in their right
mind would do such a thing, the Venezuelan

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:23.570
government has had to back this particular
cryptocurrency with oil.

00:12:23.570 --> 00:12:28.800
That is, each Petro will be guaranteed by
a barrel of oil from the Venezuelan oil reserves,

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.950
reserves that, of course, are underground.

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:48.529
In this way, the petro’s value is apparently
linked to the value of this raw material.

00:12:48.529 --> 00:12:49.529
Does that sound better?…

00:12:49.529 --> 00:12:54.511
well… just a moment, because we cannot forget
a detail, a very, very important detail:

00:12:54.511 --> 00:12:58.280
the oil reserves, my friends, are also under
the control of the government.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:02.810
And I wonder, do you really think that this
government is going to exploit those reserves?

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.650
And even if they did, do you think they’d
really back the petro?

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.420
And what about the support rate?

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:09.980
Wouldn’t the resources generated be spent?

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:13.920
Wouldn’t they impose restrictions or regulations
that would benefit them?

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:19.220
And above all, why the hell take the risk
of investing in petros?

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:22.510
By the way, an important point, the petro
isn’t convertible.

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:26.740
That is to say, even though it is supposedly
backed by oil barrels, you can never exchange

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:31.290
it for the barrel or for any title that proves
a right over those barrels.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:35.560
("The petro is a cryptocurrency that isn’t
crypto, that is backed by reserves that aren’t

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:36.560
reserves.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:40.420
That can only be monetized with a production
that is collapsing and issued by a government

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:42.930
that is in default and has no dollars."

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:46.990
Francisco Monaldi, professor at the Rice University’s
Baker Institute in Houston)

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:51.529
Folks, the petro doesn’t seem to be anything
more than a last ditch attempt to gain time

00:13:51.529 --> 00:13:56.329
and try to obtain the greatest possible number
of dollars by taking advantage of the popularity

00:13:56.329 --> 00:14:01.170
of cryptocurrencies, and perhaps of capital
laundering… because, who would put the dollars

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:04.070
on the table?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:10.300
The fact is that if this crypto doesn’t
work… and that looks like the most plausible

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:11.300
scenario…

00:14:11.300 --> 00:14:13.290
Maduro's regime will only have three options:

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:17.320
first, accept some kind of internal revolt
and leave power one way or another, which

00:14:17.320 --> 00:14:18.590
seems very difficult;

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:23.850
second, use an even tougher hand and condemn
Venezuela to an even greater humanitarian

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:24.850
disaster;

00:14:24.850 --> 00:14:28.080
or third, try to get the Chinese and Russians
to buy the country’s national resources

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:33.160
in mass and by all means, such as refineries,
oil and many other raw materials.

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:38.740
That is to say, become a kind of colony by
selling at a loss each and every one of the

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:43.079
Crown jewels so that the regime’s elite
can continue to enjoy their standard of living.

00:14:43.079 --> 00:14:47.920
Dear viewers, Nicolás Maduro and company
are still in power, and it hardly seems like

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.180
Venezuela will have a better future.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.450
But now... it’s your turn…

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.850
Would you be willing to exchange your money
for petros?

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:56.260
Leave your answer in the comments and in this
survey as well.

00:14:56.260 --> 00:15:00.480
I really hope you enjoyed this video, please
hit like if you did and don’t forget to

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:04.269
subscribe to our channel for brand new videos
every Monday and Thursday.

